- the idea is to create a process that one can implement an investment strategy and try it out on hitorical data up to now and also do now-casting
- for this to happen first there should be a mechanism that autoamtically downloads the prices of different stock from different sources (up to date) and creats a database of them and has the ability to update them on any given time
- the other piece is to "categorize" these stocks and funds and etc so that one can define strategies based on those categories if needed, e.g. in tech, health, etc, and other types of categorization 
- and the actual simulation plan that given a strategy how would it perform on stock x if started at this time and ended at this time, how would it work if it was applied to all items in category z, how would it apply to all stocks in the market etc. and then have a dashboard that increases overtime whenever a new strategy is added and allows for easy comparisons of them based on their performances with confidence intervals etc. 
- Ther should finally be a step that runs this on a daily or weekly or monthly basis on all the stock in the set and all the strategies so that the process is always done in the background and all the calculations and data are saved and the dashboards are always up to date with the possibility of answering all the quesitons above.